Title: Constrain the language set
Link: https://assemblyai.com/docs/pre-recorded-audio/code-switching#constrain-the-language-set
Page: pre-recorded-audio/code-switching
Content: ### Constrain the language set

By default, Universal-3.5 Pro auto-detects and code-switches across all [18 supported languages](#support-for-99-languages). When you already know which languages a file contains, pass the `language_codes` parameter to constrain the model to that set.

On Universal-3.5 Pro, `language_codes` accepts any number of languages, and English is **not** required:

* **Multiple languages** — for example `["en", "es", "pt"]` or `["es", "fr"]`. The model code-switches only among the languages you list.
* **A single language** — a one-element list such as `["es"]` pins transcription to that language, exactly like [`language_code`](/pre-recorded-audio/set-language-manually).
* The `language_code` returned in the response also honors your list, since the language set is passed to language identification.
* If your list includes a language Universal-3.5 Pro doesn't support, the request runs automatic language detection. If the detected language falls outside Universal-3.5 Pro's [supported set](#support-for-99-languages), the job falls through to the next model in `speech_models` (typically `universal-2`); otherwise Universal-3.5 Pro transcribes it with code switching.

<Note>
  `language_codes` is mutually exclusive with `language_code` and `language_detection`. Set only one of the three on a request.
</Note>

<CodeGroup>
  ```python title="Python SDK" {8}  expandable theme={null}
  from assemblyai.prerecorded.v2 import Transcriber, TranscriptionConfig

  # audio_file = "./local-file.mp3"
  audio_file = "https://assembly.ai/wildfires.mp3"

  config = TranscriptionConfig(
      speech_models=["universal-3-5-pro"],
      language_codes=["en", "es", "pt"],  # Constrain to English, Spanish, Portuguese
  )

  transcript = Transcriber(api_key="<YOUR_API_KEY>", config=config).transcribe(audio_file)

  if transcript.status == "error":
    raise RuntimeError(f"Transcription failed: {transcript.error}")

  print(transcript.text)
  ```

  ```python title="Python" {11}  expandable theme={null}
  import requests
  import time

  base_url = "https://api.assemblyai.com"
  headers = {"authorization": "<YOUR_API_KEY>"}

  data = {
      "audio_url": "https://assembly.ai/wildfires.mp3",
      "speech_models": ["universal-3-5-pro"],
      "language_codes": ["en", "es", "pt"],  # Constrain to English, Spanish, Portuguese
  }

  response = requests.post(base_url + "/v2/transcript", headers=headers, json=data)

  if response.status_code != 200:
      print(f"Error: {response.status_code}, Response: {response.text}")
      response.raise_for_status()

  transcript_id = response.json()["id"]
  polling_endpoint = f"{base_url}/v2/transcript/{transcript_id}"

  while True:
      transcript = requests.get(polling_endpoint, headers=headers).json()
      if transcript["status"] == "completed":
          print(transcript["text"])
          break
      elif transcript["status"] == "error":
          raise RuntimeError(f"Transcription failed: {transcript['error']}")
      else:
          time.sleep(3)
  ```

  ```javascript title="JavaScript SDK" {15}  expandable theme={null}
  import { AssemblyAI } from "assemblyai";

  const client = new AssemblyAI({
    apiKey: "<YOUR_API_KEY>",
  });

  // You can use a local filepath:
  // const audioFile = "./local-file.mp3";

  // Or use a publicly-accessible URL:
  const audioFile = "https://assembly.ai/wildfires.mp3";

  const params = {
    audio: audioFile,
    speech_models: ["universal-3-5-pro"],
    language_codes: ["en", "es", "pt"], // Constrain to English, Spanish, Portuguese
  };

  const run = async () => {
    const transcript = await client.transcripts.transcribe(params);

    if (transcript.status === "error") {
      console.error(`Transcription failed: ${transcript.error}`);
      process.exit(1);
    }

    console.log(`\nFull Transcript:\n\n${transcript.text}\n`);
  };

  run();
  ```

  ```javascript title="JavaScript" {11}  expandable theme={null}
  const baseUrl = "https://api.assemblyai.com";
  const headers = {
    authorization: "<YOUR_API_KEY>",
  };

  const data = {
    audio_url: "https://assembly.ai/wildfires.mp3",
    speech_models: ["universal-3-5-pro"],
    language_codes: ["en", "es", "pt"], // Constrain to English, Spanish, Portuguese
  };

  const url = `${baseUrl}/v2/transcript`;
  let res = await fetch(url, {
    method: "POST",
    headers: { ...headers, "Content-Type": "application/json" },
    body: JSON.stringify(data),
  });
  if (!res.ok) throw new Error(`Error: ${res.status}`);
  const response = await res.json();

  const transcriptId = response.id;
  const pollingEndpoint = `${baseUrl}/v2/transcript/${transcriptId}`;

  while (true) {
    res = await fetch(pollingEndpoint, { headers });
    if (!res.ok) throw new Error(`Error: ${res.status}`);
    const transcriptionResult = await res.json();

    if (transcriptionResult.status === "completed") {
      console.log(transcriptionResult.text);
      break;
    } else if (transcriptionResult.status === "error") {
      throw new Error(`Transcription failed: ${transcriptionResult.error}`);
    } else {
      await new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, 3000));
    }
  }
  ```
</CodeGroup>

Title: Choose a locale
Link: https://assemblyai.com/docs/pre-recorded-audio/language-detection#choose-a-locale
Page: pre-recorded-audio/language-detection
Content: ## Choose a locale

When English is detected by automatic language detection, the transcript is rendered in the default US English spelling. Set your preferred English locale to render it in a regional spelling variant instead.

* Set `language_detection_options.localization` to a locale code. The supported values are `en_au` (Australian English) and `en_uk` (British English).
* When English is detected, the transcript uses that locale's spelling — for example `colour`, `behaviour`, and `organise`.
* `language_code` in the response returns the region-aware code (such as `en_au`) instead of the base `en`.

<CodeGroup>
  ```python title="Python" for="python" highlight={21}  expandable theme={null}
  import requests
  import time

  base_url = "https://api.assemblyai.com"

  headers = {
      "authorization": "<YOUR_API_KEY>"
  }

  with open("./my-audio.mp3", "rb") as f:
    response = requests.post(base_url + "/v2/upload",
                            headers=headers,
                            data=f)

  upload_url = response.json()["upload_url"]

  data = {
      "audio_url": upload_url, # You can also use a URL to an audio or video file on the web
      "language_detection": True,
      "language_detection_options": {
        "localization": ["en_au"]
    }
  }

  url = base_url + "/v2/transcript"
  response = requests.post(url, json=data, headers=headers)

  transcript_id = response.json()['id']
  polling_endpoint = base_url + "/v2/transcript/" + transcript_id

  while True:
    transcription_result = requests.get(polling_endpoint, headers=headers).json()

    if transcription_result['status'] == 'completed':
      print(transcription_result['text'])
      print(transcription_result['language_code'])
      break

    elif transcription_result['status'] == 'error':
      raise RuntimeError(f"Transcription failed: {transcription_result['error']}")

    else:
      time.sleep(3)
  ```

  ```javascript title="JavaScript" for="javascript" highlight={24}  expandable theme={null}
  import fs from "fs-extra";

  const baseUrl = "https://api.assemblyai.com";

  const headers = {
    authorization: "<YOUR_API_KEY>",
  };

  const path = "./my-audio.mp3";
  const audioData = await fs.readFile(path);
  let res = await fetch(`${baseUrl}/v2/upload`, {
    method: "POST",
    headers,
    body: audioData,
  });
  if (!res.ok) throw new Error(`Error: ${res.status}`);
  const uploadResponse = await res.json();
  const uploadUrl = uploadResponse.upload_url;

  const data = {
    audio_url: uploadUrl, // You can also use a URL to an audio or video file on the web
    language_detection: true,
    language_detection_options: {
      localization: ["en_au"],
    },
  };

  const url = `${baseUrl}/v2/transcript`;
  res = await fetch(url, {
    method: "POST",
    headers: { ...headers, "Content-Type": "application/json" },
    body: JSON.stringify(data),
  });
  if (!res.ok) throw new Error(`Error: ${res.status}`);
  const response = await res.json();

  const transcriptId = response.id;
  const pollingEndpoint = `${baseUrl}/v2/transcript/${transcriptId}`;

  while (true) {
    res = await fetch(pollingEndpoint, { headers });
    if (!res.ok) throw new Error(`Error: ${res.status}`);
    const transcriptionResult = await res.json();

    if (transcriptionResult.status === "completed") {
      console.log(transcriptionResult.text);
      console.log(transcriptionResult.language_code);
      break;
    } else if (transcriptionResult.status === "error") {
      throw new Error(`Transcription failed: ${transcriptionResult.error}`);
    } else {
      await new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, 3000));
    }
  }
  ```
</CodeGroup>

<Note>
  **Things to know**

  * **Only applies to English.** If the detected language isn't English, transcription proceeds as normal in the detected language. The locale is applied only when the detected language is English; otherwise the request is unaffected.
  * **English only.** `en_au` and `en_uk` are the only supported locales today. Base and default-region codes such as `en` and `en_us` aren't localization variants and return a `400`.
  * **One locale per base language.** Passing both `en_au` and `en_uk` returns a `400`.
  * **Requires automatic language detection.** `localization` only applies when `language_detection` is `true`. If you already know the language, set `language_code` to `en_au` or `en_uk` directly instead.
  * **Spelling only.** Localization affects spelling, not vocabulary or grammar.
</Note>

Title: Language selection
Link: https://assemblyai.com/docs/sync-stt/language-selection
Page: sync-stt/language-selection
Content: Pass `language_codes` in the `config` part to steer transcription toward a specific language. For multilingual or code-switching audio, pass an array of codes instead of a single code.

* Accepts a single ISO language code (`"es"`) or a list of codes (`["en", "es"]`)
* When omitted, no language steering is applied
* Applies alongside a custom `prompt` — see [Specifying the language](/sync-stt/prompting-and-keyterms#specifying-the-language)

<Tabs groupId="language">
  <Tab title="Python SDK" language="python-sdk" default>
    ```python theme={null}
    from assemblyai.sync.v1 import SyncTranscriber, SyncTranscriptionConfig

    config = SyncTranscriptionConfig(model="universal-3-6-pro", language_codes=["es"])

    transcriber = SyncTranscriber(api_key="<YOUR_API_KEY>", config=config)
    transcriber.warm()  # open the connection ahead of the request
    result = transcriber.transcribe("sample.wav")
    print(result.text)
    ```
  </Tab>

  <Tab title="JavaScript SDK" language="javascript-sdk">
    ```javascript theme={null}
    import { AssemblyAI } from "assemblyai";

    const client = new AssemblyAI({ apiKey: process.env.ASSEMBLYAI_API_KEY });

    await client.sync.warm(); // open the connection ahead of the request
    const result = await client.sync.transcribe("sample.wav", {
      model: "universal-3-6-pro",
      language_codes: ["es"],
    });
    console.log(result.text);
    ```
  </Tab>

  <Tab title="Python" language="python">
    ```python theme={null}
    import json
    import requests

    with open("sample.wav", "rb") as f:
        audio = f.read()

    response = requests.post(
        "https://sync.assemblyai.com/v1/transcribe",
        headers={
            "Authorization": "<YOUR_API_KEY>",
            "X-AAI-Model": "universal-3-6-pro",
        },
        files={
            "audio": ("sample.wav", audio, "audio/wav"),
            "config": (None, json.dumps({"language_codes": ["es"]}), "application/json"),
        },
        timeout=60,
    )
    response.raise_for_status()
    print(response.json()["text"])
    ```
  </Tab>

  <Tab title="JavaScript" language="javascript">
    ```javascript theme={null}
    import { readFileSync } from "fs";

    const audio = readFileSync("sample.wav");
    const form = new FormData();
    form.append("audio", new Blob([audio], { type: "audio/wav" }), "sample.wav");
    form.append(
      "config",
      new Blob([JSON.stringify({ language_codes: ["es"] })], {
        type: "application/json",
      })
    );

    const response = await fetch("https://sync.assemblyai.com/v1/transcribe", {
      method: "POST",
      headers: {
        Authorization: "<YOUR_API_KEY>",
        "X-AAI-Model": "universal-3-6-pro",
      },
      body: form,
    });

    const result = await response.json();
    console.log(result.text);
    ```
  </Tab>

  <Tab title="cURL" language="bash">
    ```bash theme={null}
    curl -X POST https://sync.assemblyai.com/v1/transcribe \
      -H 'Authorization: <YOUR_API_KEY>' \
      -H 'X-AAI-Model: universal-3-6-pro' \
      -F 'audio=@sample.wav;type=audio/wav' \
      -F 'config={"language_codes":["es"]};type=application/json'
    ```
  </Tab>
</Tabs>

For multilingual or code-switching audio, pass `language_codes` as an array listing every expected language:

```json theme={null}
{ "language_codes": ["en", "es"] }
```

With the SDKs, list the same codes: `SyncTranscriptionConfig(language_codes=["en", "es"])` in Python, or `{ language_codes: ["en", "es"] }` in JavaScript.

